					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/timetravelingguy" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2693525); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2693525&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608137000" alt="TimetravelingGuy" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2693525)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/timetravelingguy" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2693525); return false;" >TimetravelingGuy</a></span> <span class="odate time_1478206519 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">03 Nov 2016 20:55</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2683735">
									

<p>I'm noticing that this addition suffers from the same weakness that was pointed out with the 02/03 Exchange. There's little characterization and they feel less like characters or people and more like just means of adding exposition and additional detail.</p>
<p>If this was revised a little bit and added as an addendum to the original 001 document, I don't know if you'd be losing anything. It doesn't benefit from the tale format or add anything that make the tale format necessary.</p>
<p>I'm not going to judge until it all comes out, but this is beginning to feel like one good scp stretched out needlessly to justify the novelty of a 001 Hub as a proposal.</p>

							</div>

								
					
