    <div class="post-container" id="fpc-2684101">
                      
		<div class="post" id="post-2684101">
		<div class="long">
			<div class="head">
									<div class="options">
						<a href="javascript:;" onclick="togglePostFold(event,2684101)" class="btn btn-default btn-small btn-sm">Fold</a>
					</div>
								<div class="title" id="post-title-2684101">
																		
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/timetravelingguy" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2693525); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2693525&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608137000" alt="TimetravelingGuy" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2693525)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/timetravelingguy" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2693525); return false;" >TimetravelingGuy</a></span> <span class="odate time_1478251539 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">04 Nov 2016 09:25</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2684101">
									

<p>I think the rock in my shoe is that it's a hub and it's yet to fully justify the use of a hub. The tales don't add anything that couldn't be added into the actual article. Harbringer was a strong tale that set the stage, but the rest of it feels like abstracts of the original article and sparsely expanded on. It gives the sour taste of a &quot;gimmick&quot; scp with a moderately interesting concept behind it.</p>
<p>Twisted Gears proposal for 001 is a what I'd maybe expect from a hub styled proposal. Something that warrant's breaking down the information and telling it through different mediums. In fact, Twisted Gears proposal also addresses your point on character growth. Those characters in that proposal hardly matter to the overall concept, but their distinct voices, combined with the different exposition they carry, help convey the gravity of the knowledge and the actual emotions of 001. However in this 001 proposal&#8230;</p>
<p>We've yet to see anything relating to that in these &quot;tales&quot; outside of Harbringer. Most of the suspense (again currently) is trying to be generated through the &quot;horrible scary things talked about clinically and calmly&quot; intermixed with &quot;green light on the things have gone to shit&quot; meter. There's no real reason (currently) for this story to be told using a hub. Depending on the full scope, harbinger might deserve to be included as an attached tale or the main tale, but</p>
<p>This is all my current observation, and chances are it'll change once the entire proposal is complete. (all ready when I was framing this post, another segment was added) But currently, this slow burn excitement is beginning to fizzle for me as each entry is added. I hoping it changes for me, but as it is&#8230; I don't know if I can upvote it.</p>

							</div>

								
					
